WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.460 --> 00:00:06.700
There were areas where some people would have gardens.

2
00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:13.520
There were areas where you would see people that . . . A couple of people had cattle.

3
00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:21.160
There was families that had lived next door to us . . . Well, I call it next door, it was just across the street.

4
00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:26.360
But then Entergy bought that property out and they came through with their power lines.

5
00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:32.280
So those families, they relocated, but it was just a couple of streets away from where we lived.

6
00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:37.140
And like I said, it was . . . green trees.

7
00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:43.620
You always saw somebody out doing laundry . . . Hanging their laundry on the line.

8
00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:46.680
Children getting ready to go to and from school.

9
00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:54.040
So it was a lot of activity that was going on in the area that we lived in.

10
00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:57.920
You know, as I got to be close to school age,

11
00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:07.860
I remember we started getting more neighbors to come in because for a long time we were the only family on our end of the block.

12
00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:14.340
There were a couple of other families that moved in and as they moved in they all had children.

13
00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:16.740
So that gave me an opportunity to have some playmates.

14
00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:23.200
There were some families that had moved next door to us.

15
00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:26.300
The first family was Fontenots and they moved back to Lake Charles.

16
00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:29.700
And then the Singleton family moved next door.

17
00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:37.620
Then we had the Miles family, the Reado family, and the Moutons that lived by us, so . . . And everybody was real close.

18
00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:48.480
And by my mom not working ,if any of the other mothers had a job they needed to go to then they would leave their kids with her because they knew that she would be at home.

19
00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:53.680
So I was excited because I always had somebody to play with.

20
00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:56.760
Somebody coming over.

21
00:01:56.760 --> 00:02:06.800
We would go occasionally down to the Mossville area we called across the track and we'd go to the recreation center there and play on the playground equipment.

22
00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:15.380
But otherwise we just went from house to house playing games, you know, ball, hopscotch, shooting marbles.

23
00:02:15.380 --> 00:02:20.880
I was a girl, but I had my own little sack of marbles. [laughs] My dad had taught me how to shoot marbles.

24
00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:24.300
So it was just everybody was real close knit.

25
00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:32.120
If somebody butchered, they shared the meat [laughs] with the other families.

26
00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:34.760
We all got to know each other's family members.

27
00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:41.960
If something was going on with one family, everybody would go over and see their family members or vice versa.

28
00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:45.640
They'd come over to our house if my grandmother came over to visit.

29
00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:46.940
So it was just real nice.

30
00:02:46.940 --> 00:02:53.700
It was . . . When there were shade trees we all got to play outside [laughs] under the shade trees.

31
00:02:53.700 --> 00:03:03.000
It was a community where I can remember at night you didn't have to lock your doors or windows because it was real safe.

32
00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:06.520
So everybody just . . . Once it got dark, you know,

33
00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:11.860
you went in and you took your bath and settled down for the night and that was it.

34
00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:13.880
You'd hear cars passing.

35
00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:21.520
But we still didn't have a lot of neighbors even into the early sixties, and then the community, it just continued to grow.

36
00:03:21.520 --> 00:03:23.960
There were more and more families that started coming in.
